<div>
  <img decoding="async" width="696" height="392" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_1990922204.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Bitcoin Price Regains Strength Above $41K, Crypto Market Cap Jumps 6% in 24 Hours" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>Crypto assets have climbed in value during the last 24 hours as the price of bitcoin tapped a high on Friday, reaching $42,411 per unit at 8:00 p.m. (EDT). The entire market capitalization of all 10,000+ crypto assets is $1.64 trillion on Saturday, up over 6% during the last day.</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2>
    Bitcoin Climbs Over 20% This Week
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    The price of bitcoin (BTC) and a number of other digital assets have climbed higher in value during the last few days. Five days ago, a massive short squeeze propelled the price of bitcoin higher as it jumped just below the $40K handle from a low of $34,500 per unit.
  </p><figure id="attachment_478047" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-478047" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-478047 size-full" title="Bitcoin Price Regains Strength Above $41K, Crypto Market Cap Jumps 6% in 24 Hours" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/rekts.jpg" alt="Bitcoin Price Regains Strength Above $41K, Crypto Market Cap Jumps 6% in 24 Hours" width="1280" height="250" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-478047" class="wp-caption-text">Bybit.com’s Liquidation Data.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    Similarly, there was also a large derivatives expiry on Friday ending the month of July and at around 8:00 p.m. (EDT) a swathe of short positions were liquidated. During the course of the last day, $284.7 million worth of positions were liquidated according to bybt.com’s Liquidation Data.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    After 8:00 p.m., the price of bitcoin (BTC) quickly spiked to $42,411 per unit and has remained above the $41K handle since then. BTC is up over 7% today and over 20% during the last seven days. Out of the entire $1.64 trillion, bitcoin’s (BTC) market cap captures 47.66% of the aggregate with $781 billion.
  </p><figure id="attachment_478048" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-478048" style="width: 2428px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-478048 size-full" title="Bitcoin Price Regains Strength Above $41K, Crypto Market Cap Jumps 6% in 24 Hours" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bitstamp_btc_usd-sat_31_jul_08_40_26.jpg" alt="Bitcoin Price Regains Strength Above $41K, Crypto Market Cap Jumps 6% in 24 Hours" width="2428" height="1316" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-478048" class="wp-caption-text">BTC/USD chart on July 31, 2021, via Bitstamp.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    BTC has around $33 billion in global trade volume on Saturday with tether (USDT) commanding 59% of all trades. This is followed by USD (12.29%), BUSD (5.85%), JPY (4.34%), and EUR (3.41%). At the time of writing, BTC is exchanging hands for $41,522 per unit.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <h2>
    Ethereum Spikes 12% This Week, Easyfi Jumps Over 2,800%, Tether Captures 47% of Global Trade Volume
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    The second-largest crypto asset, in terms of market cap, is ethereum (ETH) up over 5% during the last day. ETH has gained 12% during the last seven days and at press time ETH is swapping for $2,455 per unit.
  </p><figure id="attachment_478049" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-478049" style="width: 2428px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-478049 size-full" title="Bitcoin Price Regains Strength Above $41K, Crypto Market Cap Jumps 6% in 24 Hours" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/deribit_eth_usd-sat_31_jul_08_40_36.jpg" alt="Bitcoin Price Regains Strength Above $41K, Crypto Market Cap Jumps 6% in 24 Hours" width="2428" height="1316" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-478049" class="wp-caption-text">ETH/USD chart on July 31, 2021, via Deribit.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    The biggest gainers during the last seven days include the coins easyfi (EASY) up a whopping 2,854%, flexacoin (FXC) up 706%, and omix (OMX) up 500% this week. The biggest weekly losers include beetle coin (BEET) down 83%, chip (CHIP) down 54%, iov blockchain (IOV) down 51%.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    The biggest 24-hour gainer among the top ten largest crypto assets, in terms of market valuation, is polkadot (DOT) which is up 12% today and 20% during the last week. Out of the $1.64 trillion worth of crypto assets, the reported trade volume on Saturday is $84 billion. Tether (USDT) reportedly commands $57 billion or 47.36% of today’s global trade volume among all the crypto assets recorded.
  </p>
  
